  "cleanText": "Solution home \n\t\tCapium 365\n\t\tCapium 365 (Accountant)\n\n### Capium 365: User Specific Permissions\n\n\t\t\tPrint\n\n\tModified on: Thu, 19 Jun, 2025 at 11:24 AM\n\n\t\tWhile general permission levels—Administrator, Manager, and Regular User—offer a structured way to manage team access across Capium 365, there are times when individual users require more tailored control. The User Specific Permissions feature allows you to override default access levels and customise permissions for each user as needed. \n\nIf you're looking to set up overall access levels for your team, please refer to the General User Permissions Guide. That guide outlines how to manage roles more broadly before applying individual adjustments. \n\nOnce a user has been added to the system, follow the steps below to amend their permissions directly within their profile. \n\nNavigate to Capium 365 > Manage > Users > Specific User \n\nTo edit the user permissions, firstly click this drop down: \n\nThis will allow you to choose what permission ranking the user should have: Administrator, Manager or Regular User \n\nTo change what the permission allows, press the pen icon below the drop down.   \n\nThis page will pop-up:\n\nYou can change the permissions in here for that user. \n\nOnce done you can Save, Save and Exit  \n\nNote: Before assigning permissions in Capium 365, ensure that users are added to the system. After adding a user, scroll down to the bottom of their profile to configure their permissions as needed. \n\nFor detailed instructions on adding users. Please refer to adding Users Guide.  \n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tDid you find it helpful?\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tYes\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tNo\n\nSend feedback\tSorry we couldn't be helpful. Help us improve this article with your feedback.",
